1
00:00:00,027 --> 00:00:01,057
So why does this

2
00:00:01,057 --> 00:00:01,987
method work?

3
00:00:01,987 --> 00:00:04,340
it's about having somewhere to put things in

4
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:05,147
your mind.

5
00:00:05,147 --> 00:00:07,450
When you start reading a book cold,

6
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:09,950
every new idea from the book that arrives,

7
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:12,840
your brain has nowhere to file it.

8
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:16,027
So the idea sort of floats in your mind.

9
00:00:16,027 --> 00:00:17,257
And by the time you are in,

10
00:00:17,257 --> 00:00:19,050
say, chapter six,

11
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:22,170
you already have a pile of ideas

12
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:24,100
floating around in your mind,

13
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:26,983
and they have nothing to attach themselves

14
00:00:27,313 --> 00:00:28,393
But when you have

15
00:00:28,393 --> 00:00:29,833
started the structure first,

16
00:00:29,833 --> 00:00:31,656
you already know the shape of the argument.

17
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:33,974
So when an idea shows up in the book,

18
00:00:33,974 --> 00:00:36,133
you know which part of the book it belongs

19
00:00:36,133 --> 00:00:37,793
to and what it is doing there.

20
00:00:37,793 --> 00:00:38,536
In your mind,

21
00:00:38,536 --> 00:00:41,375
that idea has somewhere to go to.

22
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:43,243
That's the whole mechanism.

23
00:00:43,243 --> 00:00:44,496
You're building the

24
00:00:44,496 --> 00:00:45,133
shelves

25
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:45,736
before you

26
00:00:45,736 --> 00:00:47,735
put something on them.
